 "sentences": [
  {
   "s": 0.0,
   "e": 4.76,
   "text": "You don't have a motivation problem, you have a size problem. When a goal is too big your brain"
  },
  {
   "s": 4.76,
   "e": 9.92,
   "text": "can't see where to start, so it does the easiest thing it waits for tomorrow. Take writing a book"
  },
  {
   "s": 9.92,
   "e": 16.26,
   "text": "that's 300 pages. Nobody can start 300 pages on a Tuesday night. So shrink it until the first step"
  },
  {
   "s": 16.26,
   "e": 22.2,
   "text": "is obvious. Outline the first chapter this week, then write 300 words a day. Same with getting fit."
  },
  {
   "s": 22.64,
   "e": 27.04,
   "text": "That's the big goal so break it down. Start going to the gym and set up a program say six days a"
  },
  {
   "s": 27.04,
   "e": 31.8,
   "text": "week. Then take that program one day at a time. Today is just chess day and that's all you need"
  },
  {
   "s": 31.8,
   "e": 36.38,
   "text": "to think about. Here's a simple test. If you can't start the first step in under 15 minutes,"
  },
  {
   "s": 36.38,
   "e": 41.04,
   "text": "it's still too big break it down again. Every small step you finish gives you a little proof"
  },
  {
   "s": 41.04,
   "e": 46.18,
   "text": "that you can do it. And that proof is what motivation actually feels like. That's what"
  },
  {
   "s": 46.18,
   "e": 50.84,
   "text": "demure is for. You archive your dream today so you can see it tomorrow and break it down"
  },
  {
   "s": 50.84,
   "e": 55.54,
   "text": "into small steps you can actually do. If you want to try it out, I've put the link in the bio."
  }
 ],
